// The C ABI exports of std/time's zone data (decisions 0204, 0207): like
// cabi.xo, every top level function here is called by the C runtime as
// xo_x_<name>; std/native/time.xo imports this module, so a program that
// uses std/time (compiled with -DXO_TIME) has them.
use native/llrt/tzhost

/// Releases the zones std/native/llrt/tzhost.xo kept, at exit under
/// XO_LEAKCHECK (xo_rt.c's xo_tz_exit_free, set in xo_std.c).
fn tz_free() { tzhost.free() }
